q35 for the setup screenshots in QEMU (tools/qemu-setup-shots.py), never
in a W541 ROM: like q35-update-test.patch, it goes in a git worktree of the
coreboot tree of its own, which only builds the ROM for QEMU
(tools/q35-cfr-rom.sh).

The W541 cannot be emulated, so its setup menu cannot come from its
ramstage: tools/cfr-dump.sh builds the menu code of the W541 on the host
and writes the CFR record that the ramstage puts in the coreboot table.
With DRIVERS_OPTION_CFR, mb_cfr_setup_menu() of q35 copies that record
from the CBFS file cfr.bin into the table as it is (qemu-setup-shots.py
--cfr adds the file to its copy of the ROM with cbfstool), so the payload
of the W541 shows the W541's menu. Without the file, or with a file that
is not a CFR record, the generic forms of q35 as on any board.

